gxfte_results.md` attached and the checklist at 11 of 11. No repository files were changed and the worktree is clean.\n\n**Verdict.** No released tag and no current main of agents-management offers a native Pi runtime. Tag v0.5.10 is the main head, so there is nothing unreleased to pick up. The A0 findings hold and are stronger than reported.\n\n- The pi system plugin resolves the agents-infra wrapper as its binary, and its Preflight execs `agents-infra runtime status` on every non-dry-run launch. A native launch through it is gated by the local-model broker.\n- The agents-infra wrapper does not strip an inherited Pi home. It refuses the launch outright with `pi_execution_environment_invalid`, so a Curator-managed home can never reach Pi through it.\n- curator-spec never names agents-infra for pi. The environments protocol declares `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` as the home variable and seeds the managed home from the native one. Native Pi is the decided shape.\n\n**Pi 0.84.2 semantics** were read from the installed source and one bounded offline probe in a fresh home. Model resolution errors and invalid thinking words exit with code 1, never a silent substitution. A bare model id absent from the catalog is an error, while a `provider/id` spelling falls back to a custom model with a warning. Pi silently clamps an unsupported thinking level to the nearest supported one. The built-in anthropic catalog lacks `claude-fable-5-1`, which is the module's top row. The native home on this machine has only a llama-cpp provider and an empty auth file, so a seeded managed home has no cloud auth here.\n\n**Proposed upstream change**, additive with no schema change: a new `pi-native` system plugin that resolves raw `pi`, declares dry-run and interactive modes only, carries effort as `--thinking`, has no Preflight, and leaves the existing pi plugin untouched. Vendor rows verified in Pi's catalog gain `pi-native` membership, and three runtimes bind that system to anthropic, openai and google. The report lists the goldens, gate-narrowing negatives, and the digest-stability check to watch.\n\n**Tag prerequisite.** A signed v0.5.11 tag from the operator after the change lands, then the launcher requires it and SPEC §4.2 maps `pi` to `pi-native`.\n\n**One unavoidable decision** is the system id. I recommend a new `pi-native` id with `pi` kept for the wrapper, because the wrapper is load-bearing for local-qwen and rebinding `pi` would break existing local-models configs and goldens. Everything else has an evidence-backed default and is not a blocker.\n\nNo LOGBOOK entry was written per the operator's instruction. Probe logs are under the task's `.temp` directory in the worktree.","ttft_ms":2758,"type":"result","duration_ms":709780,"uuid":"5dbd8b5b-b37f-4525-9899-9f41d1aff6fd","ttft_stream_ms":1790,"time_to_request_ms":20,"first_content_frame_ms":2737,"queued_turn_count":0}
